      <section class="deck-slide" data-title="Leave with a repeatable workflow" data-notes="Close with the workshop progression: testing and CI/CD, security and DevSecOps, then spec-driven AI-assisted development. Ask students to share their live URL, one Git concept, and one AI-generated change they reviewed. Set the expectation that a clean, honest, working project is better than a complicated site they cannot explain.">
        <div class="slide-overline"><span>THE FOUNDATION FOR THE SERIES</span><span>14 / 14</span></div><div class="slide-heading"><p class="eyebrow">YOUR SITE KEEPS GROWING</p><h2>Four workshops. One evolving project.</h2><p class="slide-subtitle">Today's workflow becomes the foundation for quality, security, and structured AI development.</p></div>
        <div class="series-roadmap"><article class="roadmap-current"><span>01 · TODAY</span><h3>Git &amp; GitHub</h3><p>Version and publish your site.</p><b>YOU ARE HERE</b></article><div class="road-arrow">→</div><article><span>02 · NEXT</span><h3>Testing + CI/CD</h3><p>Automate checks and deployments.</p></article><div class="road-arrow">→</div><article><span>03 · THEN</span><h3>DevSecOps</h3><p>Find and fix security risks.</p></article><div class="road-arrow">→</div><article><span>04 · FINALLY</span><h3>Spec + AI</h3><p>Build a feature responsibly.</p></article></div>
